# Project Structure Guidelines

## Directory Organization
```
lib/
├── app_[name]/              # Application module (qy/achat/wuy)
│   ├── feature_[name]/      # Feature module
│   │   ├── view/           # Page views
│   │   ├── actions/        # Action event code
│   │   ├── widgets/        # Widgets
│   │   └── common_widgets/ # App-specific common components
│   ├── router_[name]/      # Application router
│   ├── controller/         # Application controller
│   ├── localization/       # Localization files
│   └── resources/         # Resource files
│       ├── icon_images/   # Icons and images
│       └── styles/        # Styles
├── common/                # Global common module
│   └── widgets/          # Global shared components
└── theme/                # Theme configuration
    └── mobile/          # Mobile theme
```

## Feature Module Structure
```
feature_name/
├── view/             # Page views
├── actions/          # State management
├── domain/          # Business logic
│   ├── model/       # Data models
│   └── service/     # Service layer
└── widget/          # Components
```

## Naming Conventions
- File naming:
  - Views: `xxx_screen.dart`
  - Components: `xxx_widget.dart`
  - Models: `xxx_model.dart`
  - Services: `xxx_service.dart`
- Class naming:
  - Views: `XxxScreen`
  - Components: `XxxWidget`
  - Models: `XxxModel`
  - Services: `XxxService`

## Development Process
1. New pages must be added to the development test page:
   `lib/app_dev/feature_dev/home/view/home_screen.dart`
2. Follow existing code structure without breaking other functionality
3. When using common components, copy to app's `common_widgets` directory if modifications are needed

## Code Organization
- Keep business logic in controllers
- Keep UI components in view and widgets directories
- Use services for API calls and external integrations
- Keep models simple and focused on data structure

## Import Organization
- Group imports in the following order:
  1. Dart and Flutter imports
  2. Third-party package imports
  3. Project imports
- Use relative imports for files in the same directory
- Use package imports for cross-module references





